Requirement:
	1. Extract data from MySQL db & load it in XML
	2. Extract data from CSV file & load it in XML
Using RepeatTemplate to execute this process for n number of times

Reference link:
https://www.toptal.com/spring/spring-batch-tutorial

Notes:
By default, Spring Batch executes all jobs it can find (i.e., that are configured as in CustomerReportJobConfig) at startup. 
To change this behavior, disable job execution at startup by adding the following property to application.properties:

spring.batch.job.enabled=false

Whether bean definition overriding, by registering a definition with the same name as an existing definition, is allowed. default value is false.
spring.main.allow-bean-definition-overriding=true 

Spring Batch Meta Data is AutoConfigured.
Need not to write the Batch configuration in spring_config.xml

 In order to make the Step Scope work we have to include following the SpringConfiguration File:
 
	<bean id="stepScope" class="org.springframework.batch.core.scope.StepScope">
    	<property name="autoProxy" value="true"/>
	</bean>

